                <pb facs="1002" n="890" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg890"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/156: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-30T14:00:00-05:00">March 30, 1935—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Your 69, March 29, 11 a.m. Department is inclined in general to agree with
                    the views and to approve suggestion for possible future action outlined in
                    paragraphs 1 and 2 but will await further report from you before issuing
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
